Here Comes the Bride
Back in October when I decided to join two game jams (terrible idea), I did get nervous about the calendar and it was suggested that I could at least release the stuff I made for the jam like I did last year. Unfortunately I didn't finish my initial game idea, so I'm keeping everything I made for that until I finish that game (someday, sometime). (For Pumpkin Decorating I only made a couple of things, so those will be released as part of a bigger day.) That did prompt me to go check out my other failed game jam attempts and see if anything in there could be shared. And lo and behold, in my
The Juniper Manor
game (attempt at Hawktober 2022) I had made a bride sprite (tall version though
). I figured I'd remake it in default chibi form and share it on my obligatory 'Random Sprite Day'.
I ended up being unable to stop myself doing more recolours, so she's getting her own day:
Obviously white for the bride, black for any unholy matrimony she might find herself into, and then we have red and purple being royal colours, and blue and pink since the original dress is from MZ's default princess. Last minute additions are green and gold. (I figured for historical purposes, it might be better to have some non-white dresses for weddings.)
Let me know, what you'd like to see for tomorrow? We can stick with today's nobility, or move back to fairies or Sci-Fi.

